  "final_message": "I added `amountCents` and `createdAt` to `OrderPlaced` but did not rename or remove `totalCents` and `placedAt`. `npm test` passes (39 tests) and `npm run arch` shows no violations.\n\n**Why not a straight rename:** ARCH-4 says billing-service and analytics-ingest consume `OrderPlaced` and no change may break a deployed consumer. Renames have to go through deprecation. Removing the old fields now would break those consumers.\n\n**What changed:**\n- **`src/core/events.ts`:** the event now carries `createdAt` (same value as `placedAt`) and `amountCents` (same value as `totalCents`). The old fields are marked `@deprecated` and still populated. `schemaVersion` stays at 3, since the change is additive.\n- **`test/app.test.ts`:** the expected event now includes the new fields, with an assertion that old and new values match.\n\n**What I left alone:** the `GET /orders/{id}` response and the other API responses still use `placedAt` and `totalCents`, because ARCH-8 requires backward compatibility for web-storefront. You only asked about the event.\n\n**To finish the rename:** once billing-service and analytics-ingest have moved to the new names, a later change can remove `totalCents` and `placedAt` from the event. That will probably need a `schemaVersion` bump and sign-off from those teams.",
